# Function Call Syntax Test

All valid function call syntaxes in CalcMark.

## Traditional Function Syntax

avg(10, 20, 30)
avg(1, 2, 3, 4, 5)
sqrt(16)
sqrt(2)

## Natural Language Function Syntax

average of 10, 20, 30
average of 1, 2, 3, 4, 5
square root of 16
square root of 2

## Functions with Expressions

x = 10
y = 20
z = 30
a = 5
b = 4

avg(x, y, z)
avg(10 + 5, 20 * 2, 30 - 10)
sqrt(x + y)
square root of (a + b)

## Nested Functions

avg(sqrt(16), sqrt(25))
sqrt(avg(1, 2, 3))
average of square root of 4, square root of 9

## Functions in Assignments

mean = avg(10, 20, 30)
root = sqrt(16)
calculated = average of 100, 200, 300
side = square root of 25

## Sum Function

sum(1, 2, 3)
sum(10, 20, 30, 40)
sum($100, $200, $300)
sum(1 kg, 500 g)
sum(1 hour, 30 minutes)
sum(10%, 20%, 30%)

## Sum with Variables

cost_a = $574200
cost_b = $650000
cost_c = $368640
total_cost = sum(cost_a, cost_b, cost_c)

## Sum Natural Language

sum of 1, 2, 3
sum of $100, $200, $300
sum of 1 kg, 500 g

## Sum with Expressions

p = 100
q = 200
r = 300
computed = sum(p * 2, q, r)

## Nested Sum and Avg

sum(avg(10, 20), avg(30, 40))
avg(sum(1, 2), sum(3, 4))

## Mixed Syntax in Same Document

Traditional syntax:
total1 = avg(1, 2, 3)

Natural language syntax:
total2 = average of 1, 2, 3

Both should produce same result:
same = total1 == total2

Traditional sum:
total3 = sum(1, 2, 3)

Natural language sum:
total4 = sum of 1, 2, 3

Both sum forms should produce same result:
same_sum = total3 == total4
